1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,700
A runaway supermassive black hole is tearing across deep space at maximum velocity.

2
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:09,230
It moves at 450,000 miles per hour, but it is not destroying everything.

3
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:13,160
Hubble astronomers caught this rogue monster twenty million light years from Earth.

4
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:17,550
Two galactic supermassive black holes merged and launched this third one outward.

5
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:21,260
Look closely at the image trail. Can you spot what it left behind?

6
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:26,550
Instead of devouring gas, its supersonic speed compresses cosmic dust into newborn suns.

7
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:30,510
It created a 200,000 light-year tail of brand new baby stars.

8
00:00:30,430 --> 00:00:34,550
Scientists realization: black holes can be cosmic mothers, not just galactic killers.

9
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:38,470
This cosmic birth machine weighs twenty million suns and will never stop.

10
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,420
Which explains why...
